# What must not reach the build context.
#
# The build stage runs `COPY . .`, so without this file everything here goes
# into an image layer. .gitignore already says which of these must never be
# committed — "never commit a database with real session/credential data" — and
# that rule had not been carried across to Docker, where the same files end up
# somewhere far easier to hand to somebody else.
#
# Each exclusion is checked against what the build actually needs: the Go
# sources, go.mod/go.sum, and web/ for the node stage.

# Runtime data. The database holds password hashes and passkey material.
/data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Build output. internal/webui/dist is deliberately excluded: the node stage
# produces it and copies it in afterwards, so the version sitting in a working
# tree is irrelevant and only ever stale.
/dist/
/vibepanel
/internal/webui/dist/
/web/dist/

# Installed by `npm ci` inside the node stage, and full of platform-specific
# binaries that would be wrong for the image anyway.
/web/node_modules/

# History and tooling. The version is passed as a build argument.
.git/
.github/
*.log

# Local scratch that has no business in an image.
/shots*/
/tmp/
